From 30139c404f59c9f312292466c2fc5fcc65efeae0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:19:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 116/116] MAS local: boot a portrait window landscape for the
 boot animation

A portrait instance's window came up portrait, but Android draws its boot
animation in the screen's own shape (SurfaceFlinger's install orientation,
ROTATION_0 on a 1280x720 screen) whatever the display rotation: the Google
logo and the first frames after it lay on their side until the display
rotation of the start took over. bootanimation's own
ro.bootanim.set_orientation_<display> is not a ro.boot.* property, so the
emulator cannot hand it in on the kernel command line, and changing
ro.surface_flinger.primary_display_orientation would change what
user_rotation means after the boot.

So the window boots in the screen's shape again, as upstream sets
hw.initialOrientation for a magic skin, and turns to the orientation
config.ini asked for once the boot animation is over:

- parse_skin_files() keeps that orientation aside when the magic skin is
  the AVD's own screen (skin_configured_initial_orientation()), and the
  window takes it as the start for the rotate button.
- The boot setting of the display rotation now waits, after `settings put`,
  until init has stopped the boot animation (init.svc.bootanim=stopped) or
  the boot has completed; then the window turns to the start the way the
  button does (keeping its centre, on the screen), and the button is enabled.

Landscape instances do not turn at all.

Test: aemu-ui-lean-window_unittests (58), aemu-ui-safe-shutdown_unittests
(17).

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#225

Change-Id: Ife405ab48e04f51e3004b236841030f0e9f69ee3
